  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "Owners converting an independent **upper-upscale** hotel in North America commonly look at brands such as **Marriott’s Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Renaissance, and Autograph Collection; Hilton’s Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Curio Collection, and Canopy; IHG’s InterContinental, Kimpton, and Hotel Indigo; Choice’s Radisson Blu, Radisson, Cambria, Ascend, and Radisson Individuals; plus independents-leaning/lifestyle options like Omni, Loews, and Accor’s Fairmont**.[1][2][3][10][15]\n\nThe brands most often associated with **conversion-friendly** opportunities are especially **Autograph Collection**, **Curio Collection**, **Radisson Blu**, **Radisson**, **Cambria**, **Ascend Hotel Collection**, **Radisson Individuals**, and **voco/Vignette** where the owner wants more flexible standards or a soft-brand fit.[1][3][7][10][15]\n\nA concise way to think about the market is:\n\n- **Marriott**: Marriott Hotels, Sheraton, Westin, Renaissance, Autograph Collection[1][14]\n- **Hilton**: Hilton Hotels & Resorts, Curio Collection, Canopy, Embassy Suites, Signia by Hilton[1][14]\n- **IHG**: InterContinental, Kimpton, Hotel Indigo, Crowne Plaza, voco[1][15]\n- **Choice**: Radisson Blu, Radisson, Cambria, Ascend Hotel Collection, Radisson Individuals[3][7][10]\n- **Other upper-upscale options**: Omni, Loews, Fairmont[1][9]\n\nIf you want, I can also narrow this to the **top 5 most realistic conversion targets** by owner profile, market type, or brand fee/standards level.",
